  "notes": "USAGE: {判断|はんだん} refers to forming conclusions or making decisions based on reasoning and evidence.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{判断|はんだん}する (to judge, to decide)\n・{判断|はんだん}を{下|くだ}す (to make a judgment)\n・{判断|はんだん}を{誤|あやま}る (to misjudge)\n・{判断|はんだん}に{迷|まよ}う (to be uncertain in judgment)\n・{判断|はんだん}に{任|まか}せる (to leave to someone's judgment)\n\nCOMMON COMPOUNDS:\n・{判断力|はんだんりょく} (judgment ability)\n・{判断|はんだん}{基準|きじゅん} (criteria for judgment)\n・{判断|はんだん}{材料|ざいりょう} (grounds for judgment)\n・{自己|じこ}{判断|はんだん} (self-judgment)\n・{価値|かち}{判断|はんだん} (value judgment)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n・{決断|けつだん} - decision (emphasizes resolve)\n・{決定|けってい} - decision (official/final)\n・{裁判|さいばん} - trial, legal judgment",
